# Firebase
#
# google-services.json is not a secret — Google documents it as safe to check in,
# and it only lets an app *receive* pushes. It stays out anyway for two reasons:
# a fork must not silently ship somebody else's Firebase project, and the build
# has to work without it (a self-hoster has no Google account, and the plugin is
# applied conditionally for exactly that reason). Whoever builds for the Play
# Store supplies their own — see docs/plans/android-app.md.
apps/mobile/android/app/google-services.json

# The service-account key the backend signs FCM requests with. This one *is* a
# secret: it can send push to every device in every club.
firebase-service-account*.json
